[2026-03-16T02:59:40.741Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CczUCWnPqg3t5rNbY5YHaL","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a complete picture. Let me compile the final findings.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\nI've successfully located and analyzed all the requested test files and the pattern they use. Here are the full paths and details:\n\n### Write-Review Test Files Found:\n\n1. **`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/write-review-context.spec.ts`** - Tests the PropertyBookingContext component for the write review page. Contains tests for property information display, guest count, total price, authentication, and various error states.\n\n2. **`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/write-review-form.spec.ts`** - Tests the ReviewForm component. Contains tests for form validation, comment input, rating submission, and integration with the trips page and user profile.\n\n3. **`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/write-review-sliders.spec.ts`** - Tests the RatingSliders component. Contains tests for slider functionality, value adjustments, range validation, and visual feedback.\n\n### Key Finding - No beforeAll Hook with truncateAndSeed:\n\nNotably, **none of the three write-review test files use a `beforeAll` hook with `truncateAndSeed`**. Instead, they:\n- Use inline `login()` and `deleteAllReviewsForGuest()` helper functions\n- Manage test state within individual tests\n- Use `test.beforeEach()` for cleanup (in write-review-form.spec.ts)\n\n### Pattern Found in Other Test Files:\n\nThe `truncateAndSeed` pattern is used in 25 other test files across the project. The standard pattern is:\n\n```typescript\nimport { test, expect } from '@playwright/test'\nimport { truncateAndSeed } from '../scripts/seed-db'\n\ntest.beforeAll(async () => {\n  const dbUrl = process.env.DATABASE_URL\n  if (dbUrl) {\n    await truncateAndSeed(dbUrl)\n  }\n})\n```\n\nThis pattern appears in files like:\n- `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/auth.spec.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/search.spec.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/property-detail.spec.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/host-dashboard-bookings.spec.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/profile-form.spec.ts`\n- And 20 others\n\n### The truncateAndSeed Function:\n\nLocated at `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/scripts/seed-db.ts`, it:\n1. Truncates all tables in dependency order (favorites, reviews, bookings, property_amenities, property_images, amenities, properties, users)\n2. Seeds the database with consistent test data (users: Emma, Alex, Sarah, Mike; properties; bookings; reviews; amenities; favorites)\n\nThe write-review tests appear to have been intentionally designed without the global database reset to handle their specific review state management needs using API calls for cleanup instead."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a69e57ad1affd65d4 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 51342\ntool_uses: 13\nduration_ms: 16552</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"401e079b-fea0-4b13-afb9-92cd0ea09018","uuid":"f2bf1f49-cdd6-4b14-a0b5-123aa0add2f8","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Find the write-review test files: write-review-context.spec.ts, write-review-form.spec.ts, write-review-sliders.spec.ts. Also find other test files in the same project that have a beforeAll hook with truncateAndSeed to understand the pattern. Return the full paths and content of all these files. Also look for the truncateAndSeed import pattern used in other spec files.","agentId":"a69e57ad1affd65d4","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a complete picture. Let me compile the final findings.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\nI've successfully located and analyzed all the requested test files and the pattern they use. Here are the full paths and details:\n\n### Write-Review Test Files Found:\n\n1. **`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/write-review-context.spec.ts`** - Tests the PropertyBookingContext component for the write review page. Contains tests for property information display, guest count, total price, authentication, and various error states.\n\n2. **`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/write-review-form.spec.ts`** - Tests the ReviewForm component. Contains tests for form validation, comment input, rating submission, and integration with the trips page and user profile.\n\n3. **`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/write-review-sliders.spec.ts`** - Tests the RatingSliders component. Contains tests for slider functionality, value adjustments, range validation, and visual feedback.\n\n### Key Finding - No beforeAll Hook with truncateAndSeed:\n\nNotably, **none of the three write-review test files use a `beforeAll` hook with `truncateAndSeed`**. Instead, they:\n- Use inline `login()` and `deleteAllReviewsForGuest()` helper functions\n- Manage test state within individual tests\n- Use `test.beforeEach()` for cleanup (in write-review-form.spec.ts)\n\n### Pattern Found in Other Test Files:\n\nThe `truncateAndSeed` pattern is used in 25 other test files across the project. The standard pattern is:\n\n```typescript\nimport { test, expect } from '@playwright/test'\nimport { truncateAndSeed } from '../scripts/seed-db'\n\ntest.beforeAll(async () => {\n  const dbUrl = process.env.DATABASE_URL\n  if (dbUrl) {\n    await truncateAndSeed(dbUrl)\n  }\n})\n```\n\nThis pattern appears in files like:\n- `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/auth.spec.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/search.spec.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/property-detail.spec.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/host-dashboard-bookings.spec.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/profile-form.spec.ts`\n- And 20 others\n\n### The truncateAndSeed Function:\n\nLocated at `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/scripts/seed-db.ts`, it:\n1. Truncates all tables in dependency order (favorites, reviews, bookings, property_amenities, property_images, amenities, properties, users)\n2. Seeds the database with consistent test data (users: Emma, Alex, Sarah, Mike; properties; bookings; reviews; amenities; favorites)\n\nThe write-review tests appear to have been intentionally designed without the global database reset to handle their specific review state management needs using API calls for cleanup instead."}],"totalDurationMs":16552,"totalTokens":51342,"totalToolUseCount":13,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9815,"cache_read_input_tokens":40783,"output_tokens":737,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9815},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
